{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124709-help-doing-translation-of-w20-to-v20","id":1124709,"title":"Help doing \"translation\" of W20 to V20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-04T05:30:12-07:00","id":1124709,"title":"Help doing \"translation\" of W20 to V20","content":"I'm trying to build all of the splats in a more cohesive and colourful way within the V20 and DAV20 mechanics. V20 for example has &quot;Lupines&quot; in its appendix, whose powers are simplified as Disciplines, with young lupines and elder lupines etc. I found this sufficient, but also sort of lacking. The Werewolves in V20 are Random Encounters, they don't really have any spirit to them.<br /> <br /> As a basic concept Garou get the different forms (Glabro, Crinos etc.) and they get the three Physical Disciplines as &quot;in-clan&quot; for EXP purposes. All Werewolves have the innate potential to be combat monsters. &quot;Blood&quot; is replaced with Rage, and Humanity (and Generation, but only kind of) with Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Each Tribe also gets a 4th Discipline as &quot;in-tribe&quot;; I was thinking Red Talons could have Animalism, Silver Fangs could have Presence etc. Theurgy is reskinned Blood Magic, with existing Rites becoming Rituals.<br /> <br /> Two things that I'd really appreciate help with:<br /> <br /> - Firstly, what 4th Discipline would you apply to each of the Garou Tribes?<br /> <br /> - Secondly, what mechanical stuff do you love so much that you'd HAVE to salvage it? I'm keeping the healing factor of Crinos for example, and I'm open to keeping Backgrounds, Merits and certain Gifts (as long as they can be made into a linear Discipline), but it would be great to have a Werewolf player's perspective on this.<br /> <br /> For example, in WTA you can't learn a Gift beyond your Rank. I'd be open to the idea that some powers are off-limits unless you reach a certain social criterion, such as spirits only teaching some supernatural merits and Discipline powers (and Combination powers, which could imitate many of the Gifts) when you have a certain Gnosis (Gnosis will have a &quot;hierarchy of sin&quot; based around the Litany and the spiritual purpose of Garou, with alternatives for BSDs and Fera) level or something along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-04-2017, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:53:30-07:00","id":1124740,"title":"","content":"Disciplines do not really work for Garou but, if you are going with the route, Garou should have probably have Koldunic Sorcery as an 'in-Clan' Discipline, rather than having Thaumaturgy, because of the connection to the spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:00:37-07:00","id":1124745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124709-help-doing-translation-of-w20-to-v20?p=1124740#post1124740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disciplines do not really work for Garou but, if you are going with the route, Garou should have probably have Koldunic Sorcery as an 'in-Clan' Discipline, rather than having Thaumaturgy, because of the connection to the spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they could, with work. There's a Gift that shuts off pain. That's simple enough; a Combination power of Auspex 1 (control of senses) and Fortitude 3 (resilient form) makes a Level 2 &quot;Gift&quot;. You pay 12 EXP and now you can ignore wound penalties up until Crippled. There's a gift that gives you a predatory animalistic sexual charisma for seduction. Animalism 3 + Presence 1. There's a gift that lets you pop claws while still in Homid form; that's just Protean 2, simple enough.<br /> <br /> One of the innate advantages of Werewolves could be that they pay half EXP for Combination Disciplines (Gifts in their terminology), but each of the Combos is taught by a different type of Spirit and you can't learn one which has a level going beyond your Gnosis divided by 2 (rounding up).<br /> <br /> Well Theurgy would be &quot;blood magic&quot; reskinned, not &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot;. Blood Magic includes Koldunism, Thaumaturgy and Necromancy, along with various types of Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-04-2017, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:08:25-07:00","id":1124839,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can really do werewolves justice by converting their gifts, shifting abilities, gnosis, etc. into a vampire character sheet. What's more important, in my opinion, is how the gifts, attacks, etc. would affect your vampire characters. I think your NPC werewolves should be built on W20 character sheets, and you should focus on translating the in-game effects rather than the character sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:22:47-07:00","id":1125037,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are just antagonists in the Vampire chronicles, don't need too much attention. Also, animalism isn't really an appropriate discipline, since they scare the hell away from all the animals because of their rage value.<br /> <br /> The V20 manual is made to help people understand that they absorb aggravated damage and can land four attacks each round, but if you want more than that just build them with the actual W20 rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}